Original commit body from da92e7bc6077f172b03d9229adf8a66c8f0995c8:

`_external_constructor_type`'s attribute branch required the constructor's
base to be a bare `ast.Name`. For `http.client.HTTPConnection(h)` the base is
itself an `ast.Attribute`, so the branch was structurally unreachable no matter
what the table held, and every method on those types stayed untyped.

The branch now unwinds the whole chain through the existing
`_unwind_attribute_chain`, which SUBSUMES the single-segment case rather than
sitting beside it: `socket.socket` unwinds to a one-element chain and takes the
same path. One rule, not two that drift. Depth is not special-cased anywhere.

THE PARITY TEST THAT SHOULD HAVE CAUGHT THIS PASSED THROUGHOUT. It asserts the
TABLE holds a key; this was a RESOLUTION defect. Table coverage and reachability
were never the same claim. The new assertion runs the live catalogue through
production's own import extraction and the real resolver.

THE ITEM'S HEADLINE FIGURE WAS INFLATED 3.4x AND IS CORRECTED. WI-lifol was
filed at "41 primitives"; 29 of those are `django.db.models`, which is a MODULE,
not a constructible type -- `models(...)` constructs nothing and no constructor
fix can reach them. They already reach production through the `.objects.`
dispatch (WI-sozoj: 447 `filter` + 121 `get` chains on pretix). The probe scored
a call form that cannot exist. Honest scope: 12 primitives across 4 types.

REAL-CODE FLOOR, measured before building (a generated probe is a ceiling, and
this log has recorded that confusion four times). Over the 103 corpus files
naming these types, counting only the JOINED shape that can mint a boundary:
dotted 10 production / 21 test; bare 4 production / 13 test. The dotted form is
the MORE common of the two here. The ten production sites are genuine net_send.

DIRECTION A/B AT THE ANALYZER, 8 repos: 60 call edges retyped, 0 lost, 0 net
change in edge count -- every "gain" pairs with a "loss" because these are the
SAME edges moving from `external.<method>` to `<Type>.<method>`. Three neutral
controls (django, pretix, kserve) moved 0/0; django is the one that matters,
since that is where a spurious `django.db.models` mint would show up.

END-TO-END through the real CLI, because retyping an edge is not the same claim
as minting a boundary: envoy 631 -> 632 chains, +1 net_send /
http.client.HTTPConnection.request, 0 lost. Each arm ran under its own fresh
XDG_CACHE_HOME so neither could be served the other's map. Verified on ONE repo;
30 of the 60 retyped edges land on a catalogued method, which is the ceiling for
boundary gain before the production/test split cuts it further.

RESIDUAL, STATED NOT IMPLIED CLOSED: `module_imports` is file-scoped, so a local
binding shadowing an imported module name is still mistyped. That already
mistyped `socket.socket(h)` at depth 1; this widens the exposure rather than
introducing it. Filed as INV-dulum and pinned by an xfail(strict=True) so a
scope-aware fix goes RED.

Two instrument controls failed first and each caught a real bug: the floor
scanner shared one variable map across the file, so two functions both naming a
connection `conn` collided and the last binding won -- mis-attributing the very
FORM it exists to measure; and the end-to-end arm discriminator matched BOTH
arms twice. A discriminator that is not unique to the change is not a control.

Instruments in-repo: scripts/measure-dotted-ctor-floor.py,
scripts/measure-dotted-ctor-resolution-ab.py.

